{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":12732453,"ns":0,"title":"Bachmann–Howard ordinal","extract":"In mathematics, the Bachmann–Howard ordinal (also known as the Howard ordinal, or Howard–Bachmann ordinal) is a large countable ordinal.\nIt is the proof-theoretic ordinal of several mathematical theories, such as  Kripke–Platek set theory (with the axiom of infinity) and the system CZF of constructive set theory.","description":"Large countable ordinal","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}